# Skills routing

## How to use (with execution-router)

**Read this file** when the turn is BA-related or matches an intent below. Load **one primary** skill. Load a **second** only when intents are clearly complementary (e.g. workshop design + Miro board analysis). On conflicts, the more specific row wins. Never bulk-load all BA sub-skills. Report loads per execution-router §3.

## Routing table

When a task matches an intent below, **open and follow** the corresponding skill under `~/.cursor/skills/<skill-folder>/SKILL.md`. Users should not have to type the skill name if the intent is clear.

| Intent | Canonical skill folder | Notes |
|--------|-------------------------|--------|
| "interactive HTML flowchart", "clickable flow diagram", "HTML diagram I can send to stakeholders", "interactive process flow" | `ba-assistant` reference: `references/visual-output-format.md` (§5, §9, §14) + `references/templates/flowchart.html` | Produce an interactive HTML flowchart from the template — design system and detail panel stay as-is; replace header, stats, nodes, edges, and the nodes JS object with real content. Save to `<initiative-folder>/visuals/<slug>.html`. |
| Draft email, Slack, Teams, Confluence copy in the BA's voice | `[your-voice-and-style rule]` (create your own per CUSTOMIZATION.md) | Load your voice rule when drafting comms or stakeholder-facing prose |
| Stakeholder `.md` (enablement, comms, debriefs, outputs) | `markdown-readability` rule + ref | Load `rules/markdown-readability.mdc` + `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/references/markdown-readability.md` |
| Confluence publish/update/wiki/docs | `publish-docs-to-confluence` | Read `mcps/` schemas first |
| Data analysis, metrics, queries, evidence for a requirement or rating, synthesis of findings | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-data-investigation` | The only data skill in this package. Uses whatever data MCPs the BA has configured. |
| Jira [YOUR-PROJECT] on [your-instance]: Bug / Story / Spike create or format | `[your-jira-templates]` (create your own — see CUSTOMIZATION.md §2, §5) | Read example issues from your project via MCP first; see `references/jira-ticket-format.md` for the generic template structure |
| **BA Assistant**, `/ba-assistant`, initiative lifecycle (intake → playback), `/next` `/status` `/report` `/publish-status` | `ba-assistant` | Orchestrator for BA workspaces. Reads specialist `ba-*` skills by path. End with **AskQuestion** at genuine decision points (see agent-behavior); Confluence **read-only** unless user asks to publish |
| Install BA Assistant from GitHub URL, "set up the BA skill package", `/install-ba-assistant` | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-install` | Then hand off to `ba-setup`. File copy is required before personalisation. |
| `/setup`, "reconfigure BA assistant", first-run personalisation | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-setup` | Writes `ba-assistant-config.mdc`; free-text in chat, not AskQuestion chips |
| BA intake / PM all-in-one review only | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-intake-reviewer` | Narrow scope; still prefer orchestrator for full flow |
| BA discovery & requirements depth | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-discovery-and-requirements` | |
| BA feature slicing & sequencing | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-feature-slicing-and-sequencing` | |
| BA solution options & ADRs | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-solution-shaping` | |
| BA epics/stories/DoR | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-story-writing` | DoR is the closing section within story-writing |
| BA RAID / living tracker | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-risk-and-tracker` | |
| BA requirements interrogation — "we need X", "the requirement is Y", "can we add Z", requirement change mid-flight, in-flight impact assessment | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-requirements-interrogator` | Runs before `ba-discovery-and-requirements` writes anything; also invoke when a requirement changes after design/code exists |
| BA project canvas, `/canvas`, "project dashboard", "visual status", "generate canvas" | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-project-canvas` | Interactive tabbed canvas; also triggered by `/status` within BA Assistant sessions |
| `/handover`, "hand this to devs", "package for delivery", "create a spike request", "raise an ADR request", "publish confirmed requirements to the repo", "give the devs the requirements" | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-dev-handover` | Publisher + gate. Derives dev-facing handover artefacts from the confirmed register; writes to the shared repo; feeds Jira. Never publishes unconfirmed work. |
| `/workshop launch`, prep a workshop | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-workshop-design` | Launch mode |
| `/close`, close out an initiative, archive an initiative, "this one's done" | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-initiative-closeout` | One-way: closure retro first, then batched file audit, then archive move. Never automatic. |
| Commitment scan, chat/Teams/Outlook promises, EOD reconciliation of messages | `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/sub-skills/ba-commitment-scan` | Read-only. DMs, replies, mentions, reacted threads. Never post. |
| `/validate-state`, `/sync-check` (retired alias), "is everything in sync", "check sync", "what's out of date" | Follow `sync-gates.mdc` → `/validate-state` path | `/validate-state` checks this chat against the current initiative. Write what this chat captured into the right files: `SESSION-CONTEXT.md`, the tracker, and `status-data.json` where those files already exist, and upsert only the BA actions that came from this chat into `~/.cursor/_workstream/ba-actions.json`. Do not refresh the workboard. Do not walk every open action. Do not invent files. If something has no obvious home, say so and ask. |
| `/wrap`, "wrap up", "checkpoint", "close out this chat", "close out this thread" | Follow `~/.cursor/commands/wrap.md` | Chat-scoped checkpoint: capture this thread's decisions/actions/outputs, promote its unpromoted items, **sync-ba-actions** for actions changed here only (see `references/ba-actions-format.md`), checkpoint SESSION-CONTEXT. Not a retro. Does not refresh the workboard or reconcile the calendar — that is `/workboard end-of-day`. |
| "done for tonight", "I'm done for the day", "end of day", `/workboard end-of-day` | `~/.cursor/commands/workboard.md` → `references/eod-closeout-procedure.md` | End of day. Never loads `ba-retrospective-and-learning`; a retro runs only on `/retro` or an explicit request. |
| `/workboard`, "what should I work on", "my priorities", "what's next across everything", "show me my tasks", "update the workboard" (canvas Update button) | Follow `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/references/workboard-procedure.md` + `workboard-format.md` + `ba-actions-format.md` | Cross-initiative workboard — **full refresh** (inline procedure, not a sub-skill). Distinct from `ba-project-canvas`. |
| `/todo`, "add to my to-do list", "quick task", "reminder to", `/done`, `/todo list`, "show my to-dos" | Follow `todo-quick-capture.mdc` | Quick-capture personal tasks into `_workstream/ba-actions.json`; regenerate `ba-actions.md`. No orchestrator, no ceremony. |

If two skills seem relevant, prefer the **more specific** row (e.g. project Jira templates before generic Jira). When unsure, ask one clarifying question rather than loading every skill.
